# The Kid: never a joke, never a threat. Two conversations: the name, and an ask while lost. A
# promise to get them home (walk.) is kept by the world: when the Kid is settled at a house.

conv wanderer.kid.name
for wanderer:kid
topic "Ask the kid's name."
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say "My mum said not to tell people my name. Then she said if I'm lost, tell a grown-up. I don't know which one you are."
  > @mine "Here's mine first." -> name
  > @ok "That's fine. Keep it." -> keep

node name
  say "Okay. That's fair. You can call me what my class called me. It's not very nice, so I won't say it."
  say "I'm hungry, but I'm not supposed to say that either."
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node keep
  say "Thank you."
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.kid.home
for wanderer:kid
when kidlost
topic "Ask where home is."
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say "There was a gym. With a bear on the door. They said they'd come back for the ones outside."
  say "I waited. Then it got dark, so I walked."
  > @show "I'll show you the way to a house." -> walk
  > @promise "I'll get you home. I promise." -> walk   do promise:walk.home:3h
  > @later "Stay here. Someone will come." -> wait

node walk
  say "Is it far? I can walk far. I just can't walk at night."
  do call:slot:0
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node wait
  say "Everyone says that."
  > @show2 "I'll show you the way after all." -> walk
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub
